        "text": "Current-release adjustment: the level effect from April's energy-price-cap fall has already entered the annual rate, while May's headline was unchanged at 2.8%. Transport and services are the main upside mechanism, but goods, food, and household-services easing keep the central forecast below 3.0% unless June air fares, fuel, or package holidays are unusually strong."
      },
      {
